{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794478384,"nonce":"tfHYT7dqH3HnqmjT4YZYJhPhhqg=","message":"Direction refined by the user on 2026-11-12: the goal is to reuse existing C/C++ libraries and get both Rust bindings and Haxe bindings for them automatically. This replaces steps 3 and 4 of the plan above.\n\nRevised pipeline:\n\n1. Header -\u003e WebIDL, as before (libclang or bindgen's parser).\n2. The WebIDL is edited and committed, as before: ownership, nullability, out-parameters, array lengths, callback lifetime, error conventions as extended attributes.\n3. **WebIDL -\u003e a Rust crate.** Generate `extern \"C\"` declarations (or use bindgen's output for them) plus a safe Rust API over them: an opaque C handle becomes a struct that frees it in `Drop`, a function becomes a method, an error code becomes a `Result`, a pointer and length become a slice or `Vec`, a callback becomes `impl Fn`. The API is marked with `#[hxn::interface]`, `#[hxn::methods]` and `#[hxn::data]`, and links the C library from its build script.\n4. **Haxe bindings come from that crate** through the existing pipeline (`hxn build`, `hxn package`), with no change to hxn-gen.\n\nWhy this shape: a Rust user gets a usable safe crate, the Haxe side needs no second front end in hxn-gen, and everything the Rust path supports (futures, typed errors, collection hints, every runtime) is available to wrapped C libraries. The generated crate can also be edited by hand where the WebIDL cannot express what the library does.\n\nNew open questions:\n- Whether the generated crate is regenerated on every build (a build script) or generated once and committed for hand-editing. Probably both: generated, with an override file.\n- Linking the C library for every runtime hxn supports, including wasm (needs the C library compiled for that target) and cross-compiled hxcpp targets.\n- How much of a C++ API (classes, overloads, templates, exceptions) maps onto what crosses; C++ may need a generated `extern \"C\"` shim first.","files":null}]}